WEBVTT

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:12.708
Professor Bitch, those presents
we got yesterday are fantastic!

00:00:12.708 --> 00:00:16.708
Yeah, our new P.E. gear
really kicks things up a notch!

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:20.500
I proposed a design for those, you know.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:20.875
That Karasuma wanted the same style for both boys <i>and </i>girls!

00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:21.875
"The Karasuma"
That Karasuma wanted the same style for both boys <i>and </i>girls!

00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:22.917
"The Karasuma" "The Irina"
That Karasuma wanted the same style for both boys <i>and </i>girls!

00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:24.125
"The Karasuma" "The Irina" "The Compromise"
That Karasuma wanted the same style for both boys <i>and </i>girls!

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:26.167
"The Karasuma" "The Irina" "The Compromise"
Sure glad we didn't go with the Irina.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.792
"The Karasuma" "The Irina" "The Compromise"
It's cute, but short on defense.

00:00:28.792 --> 00:00:32.375
That man just doesn't get women.

00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:35.542
He never even gave me a present!

00:00:35.542 --> 00:00:37.083
Huh?

00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:42.000
Oh, that's right: four days ago, October 10...

00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:45.583
Professor Bitch's birthday!

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.167
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:05.000
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.458
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:01:10.458 --> 00:01:13.125
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:01:13.125 --> 00:01:15.833
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:19.625
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:23.625
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:26.583
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:31.792
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:37.375
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:42.792
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:01:42.792 --> 00:01:48.292
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:01:48.292 --> 00:01:50.917
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:53.625
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:56.417
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:59.000
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.708
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:04.417
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:07.250
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:12.208
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:02:15.958 --> 00:02:19.958
"Seventh Period: Reaper Time, Part 1"
"by Meg Kataoka"

00:02:21.792 --> 00:02:22.875
Before this,

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:28.167
I've had plenty of sugar daddies
give me all kinds of pricey gifts.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.625
But now,

00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:31.083
"Karasuma" "Irina"
But now,

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:36.750
"Karasuma" "Irina"
any gift not from him is just so much worthless junk.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:37.375
any gift not from him is just so much worthless junk.

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:40.500
<i>And </i>I still can't get a hold of Lovro.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.625
Ugh. Nothing worse than being alone.

00:02:44.625 --> 00:02:48.250
Professor Bitch,
teach us more French conversation!

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:52.917
Meg... That's right: you wanted
to work overseas, didn't you.

00:02:52.917 --> 00:02:55.667
Yes--kind of, I think.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:58.208
Oh, all right, then. Have a seat--

00:02:58.208 --> 00:03:01.625
Say, the weather's so nice, let's do it outside!

00:03:01.625 --> 00:03:02.792
Huh? Why--

00:03:02.792 --> 00:03:05.125
C'mon, now, let's go!

00:03:05.958 --> 00:03:09.292
Geez, if we weren't here to push 'em along...

00:03:09.292 --> 00:03:12.250
We've successfully separated those two.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:16.292
Fingers crossed for
the birthday-present-buying squad.

00:03:16.292 --> 00:03:21.667
Professor Bitch probably already got
just about every gift there is.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.292
It's a tough one.

00:03:23.292 --> 00:03:27.042
The class pitched in 5,107 yen.

00:03:27.042 --> 00:03:28.917
--Will that even get us a present for a grown woman?

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:31.708
--I knew it! Hey, you guys!
--Will that even get us a present for a grown woman?

00:03:32.042 --> 00:03:34.333
"Flower Angel"
Did everything turn out okay?

00:03:34.333 --> 00:03:38.292
"Flower Angel"
You know, with the old guy's leg?

00:03:38.292 --> 00:03:41.125
The flower-shop guy
who called the ambulance!

00:03:41.125 --> 00:03:45.750
Thanks so much for your help.
He managed to forgive us.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:49.208
Ah. I'm glad it wasn't anything serious.

00:03:49.208 --> 00:03:53.167
And now you'd like to find a gift,
something for a grown-up?

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.667
Oh, uh-huh.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.625
How about something like this?

00:03:58.083 --> 00:04:00.167
I get it: a bouquet!

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:00.417
"Flower Angel"
I get it: a bouquet!

00:04:00.417 --> 00:04:03.292
"Flower Angel"
In an age where we have our pick of presents,

00:04:03.292 --> 00:04:07.542
"Flower Angel"
why do you think flowers are still a popular go-to gift?

00:04:07.542 --> 00:04:08.500
"Flower Angel"

00:04:08.833 --> 00:04:10.750
It's not just about heart.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:14.708
Their color, shape, fragrance--
and their impermanence--

00:04:14.708 --> 00:04:17.667
makes them a perfect match
for the human instinct.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.542
Wow, that's pretty persuasive!

00:04:20.542 --> 00:04:22.750
A very fine speech indeed...

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.750
...if only you weren't holding a calculator.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.667
Well, uh, it <i>is </i>a business...

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.542
So what'll it be?

00:04:29.542 --> 00:04:33.125
It's flowery fate! I'll even cut you a deal.

00:04:37.542 --> 00:04:42.375
And then what?
What magic word slays French guys?

00:04:42.375 --> 00:04:47.000
Geez, Toka, you're hanging on
my every word today.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.250
I'm just really curious, that's all!

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.750
Professor Bitch, play piano
for us later, like you did before!

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.167
Professor Bitch,
strike one of your killer poses!

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.250
No fair! I was first!

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.833
What--

00:04:59.833 --> 00:05:04.292
What's with me today? I'm so popular!

00:05:04.292 --> 00:05:08.125
All right, bring it on!
I'll deal with every last one of you!

00:05:08.125 --> 00:05:12.125
Just try not to get turned on,
you rotten brats!

00:05:12.125 --> 00:05:15.500
A bouquet for Irina's birthday?

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:19.500
Why me? She'd be happier to get it from you.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.875
Wow. Is he really that clueless?

00:05:23.875 --> 00:05:28.750
Mr. Karasuma, if you
consider that bitch a vital asset,

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:32.583
wouldn't winning your colleague
over be a big part of your job?

00:05:32.583 --> 00:05:36.792
Oh, and let's not tell her
who got the bouquet.

00:05:36.792 --> 00:05:39.083
You do have a point.

00:05:39.083 --> 00:05:43.750
All right, I'll do it.
Thank you for your concern.

00:05:45.917 --> 00:05:48.000
"Prep OK"

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.750
--Professor Bitch, we just remembered
something we have to do.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.542
--Huh? Wait--
--Sorry--maybe next time!

00:05:52.542 --> 00:05:56.417
Hey! Why's everyone leaving all of a sudden?

00:05:56.417 --> 00:05:59.625
What <i>is </i>all this?

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.250
I just don't get it.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.667
It's looped right back
to being a lonely day again!

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:07.125
Hey, Karasuma, listen to this!

00:06:07.125 --> 00:06:11.167
--Those brats--
--Nice timing, Irina.

00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:12.833
Karasuma?

00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:16.042
Happy birthday.

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.458
No way...

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.167
From you?

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:28.250
Sorry I'm late. Things got busy.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:34.542
I'm just thrilled. Thank you.

00:06:34.542 --> 00:06:39.625
Well done--for you, I mean. You don't
have anything up your sleeve, do you?

00:06:39.625 --> 00:06:42.125
I do want to mark the occasion.

00:06:42.125 --> 00:06:46.458
This is probably our first
and last birthday celebration.

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:52.542
What do you mean, "our first and last"?

00:06:52.542 --> 00:06:57.167
It stands to reason.
Either our mission ends or the world does.

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:58.750
One of the two.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:02.708
Either way, it'll all be over
in less than half a year.

00:07:06.792 --> 00:07:08.333
Uh-oh.

00:07:08.333 --> 00:07:09.625
You caught us.

00:07:09.625 --> 00:07:12.083
I figured it was something like this.

00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:17.917
No way would that square think
to give me flowers for my birthday.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.167
Did you enjoy yourselves?

00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:26.500
Stringing along a pro assassin,
watching her get her hopes up?

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.125
That's not it, Miss Irina.

00:07:29.125 --> 00:07:31.292
The students acted out of pure affection to--

00:07:31.292 --> 00:07:34.250
Save your lame argument, octorazzi!

00:07:36.083 --> 00:07:38.083
I remember now.

00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:41.375
This is merely a business relationship.

00:07:41.375 --> 00:07:47.292
I've just been playing school
with these brats in their peaceful world.

00:07:47.292 --> 00:07:49.875
You've opened my eyes.

00:07:49.875 --> 00:07:53.167
Thanks for the best present ever.

00:07:54.458 --> 00:07:57.333
--Hey--
--Professor Bitch!

00:07:57.833 --> 00:08:02.125
Mr. Karasuma, wasn't that a little cold?

00:08:02.125 --> 00:08:05.917
Don't tell us you still haven't noticed!

00:08:05.917 --> 00:08:08.125
Do I really look that dense to you?

00:08:08.125 --> 00:08:09.625
Huh?

00:08:09.625 --> 00:08:14.875
You may think I'm heartless,
but if she can't keep her cool,

00:08:14.875 --> 00:08:17.750
I'll hire another assassin.

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:23.042
She's not qualified to work here
if her blade can be blunted by romance.

00:08:23.042 --> 00:08:25.125
That's all there is to it.

00:08:26.542 --> 00:08:29.042
Mr. Karasuma...

00:08:29.042 --> 00:08:31.958
Argh, dammit! That pisses me off!

00:08:31.958 --> 00:08:34.792
That Kara--no, Crapsuma, that Crapsuma!

00:08:34.792 --> 00:08:37.042
Ugh, it's so hard to say!

00:08:38.708 --> 00:08:42.167
But perhaps the time has come...

00:08:42.167 --> 00:08:48.750
Given my power, there may be
nothing left for me if I stay.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:57.083
Professor Bitch hasn't come to school since.

00:08:57.083 --> 00:08:58.833
Day three, huh?

00:08:58.833 --> 00:09:02.458
Maybe we went too far.

00:09:02.458 --> 00:09:06.250
Call me if anything happens with Miss Irina.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:09.792
I've got to get to Brazil
to take in a soccer match!

00:09:09.792 --> 00:09:11.417
Samba-bye!

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:15.583
That's right--he'd had his mind set
on attending this game for a while now.

00:09:15.583 --> 00:09:20.375
"Koro Sensei's Weak Point #28: Not quite sure what 'our soccer' is"
He's your typical once-every-four-years sudden fan.

00:09:20.375 --> 00:09:21.333
He's your typical once-every-four-years sudden fan.

00:09:21.333 --> 00:09:24.083
I wonder if Professor Bitch is okay.

00:09:24.083 --> 00:09:26.917
No good. I can't get through.

00:09:26.917 --> 00:09:31.583
There's no sign of her on GPS
or public surveillance cameras.

00:09:31.583 --> 00:09:35.292
She wouldn't leave over
something like this, would she?

00:09:35.292 --> 00:09:36.958
That's not it.

00:09:36.958 --> 00:09:39.417
There's still something you need her to do.

00:09:39.417 --> 00:09:42.958
Right? And besides,
it's fun having her around.

00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:47.917
Yes, you've bonded nicely, you and her.

00:09:47.917 --> 00:09:50.917
My preliminary research
has already verified that much.

00:09:50.917 --> 00:09:54.167
All I'll do is exploit that.

00:09:59.417 --> 00:10:01.167
It was so casual,

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:06.417
the way this man just
insinuated himself into our classroom.

00:10:06.417 --> 00:10:10.333
I'm the assassin known as the Reaper.

00:10:10.333 --> 00:10:14.542
And now I have a lesson for you all.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:20.000
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season"
"by Nagisa Shiota"

00:10:24.167 --> 00:10:26.208
What the--

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.125
This guy...

00:10:29.125 --> 00:10:33.667
A flower's beauty negates human caution

00:10:33.667 --> 00:10:35.750
and opens the heart.

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:39.250
Just like I told you guys, Nagisa.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:45.250
But the original reason flowers evolved
to be lovely and fragrant--

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:49.208
Ritsu, bring up the image I sent you.

00:10:51.458 --> 00:10:54.208
--was to attract insects.

00:10:54.208 --> 00:10:55.750
Professor Bitch!

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.667
I'll cut to the chase:

00:10:57.667 --> 00:11:00.000
If you want to keep her alive,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.958
you must all come to the location I specify--

00:11:03.958 --> 00:11:06.708
and not a word to your teachers.

00:11:06.708 --> 00:11:12.833
You don't have to if you
don't want to. I can send her to you.

00:11:12.833 --> 00:11:17.250
To each of you, equally, in little pieces.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:20.125
And my next flower

00:11:20.125 --> 00:11:23.583
will likely be one of you.

00:11:23.583 --> 00:11:25.833
We couldn't see him coming.

00:11:25.833 --> 00:11:27.750
That's when I first realized

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:32.083
I was actually most afraid of not being afraid.

00:11:33.667 --> 00:11:35.708
Hey, now, buddy--

00:11:35.708 --> 00:11:41.542
we have no real obligation
to save that bossy bitch. Plus...

00:11:41.542 --> 00:11:44.667
...did you think we wouldn't
give you a beatdown right here,

00:11:44.667 --> 00:11:46.250
you kidnapper?

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:51.333
That's incorrect, Terasaka.
Wrong on all counts.

00:11:51.333 --> 00:11:55.708
You all like her more than you think.

00:11:55.708 --> 00:12:00.708
And a human could never
cut down the Reaper.

00:12:01.875 --> 00:12:07.125
Fear not. The Reaper only cuts people down.

00:12:14.958 --> 00:12:20.875
"Come as a class to the location
on the map before 6:00 tonight."

00:12:20.875 --> 00:12:24.083
"Tentacle"
Just like with Takaoka and Shiro.

00:12:24.083 --> 00:12:27.958
"Tentacle"
They must be looking to take us hostage and draw out Koro Sensei.

00:12:27.958 --> 00:12:28.667
They must be looking to take us hostage and draw out Koro Sensei.

00:12:28.667 --> 00:12:30.542
Dammit!

00:12:30.542 --> 00:12:32.375
We usin' these?

00:12:34.083 --> 00:12:35.125
"Tentacle"

00:12:35.125 --> 00:12:38.083
"Tentacle"
To protect someone... right?

00:12:38.083 --> 00:12:41.042
Greatest assassin or not,

00:12:41.042 --> 00:12:44.917
we won't let his plans go off without a hitch!

00:12:51.125 --> 00:12:53.208
Is that the way in?

00:12:53.208 --> 00:12:57.250
I did a loop-around from above.
No sign of anyone in the area.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.000
Pretty ominous...

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:02.042
Ritsu, if we're not back by midnight,

00:13:02.042 --> 00:13:04.250
tell Koro Sensei what's going on.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:07.708
I will. Stay safe, everyone.

00:13:07.708 --> 00:13:09.333
Let's go!

00:13:23.208 --> 00:13:26.000
Big space he's got here.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:27.542
That's all of you?

00:13:27.542 --> 00:13:29.917
Okay, then: I'm closing it up.

00:13:31.167 --> 00:13:35.417
Hmm. So you can tell what we're doing.

00:13:35.417 --> 00:13:38.208
"Reaper"? More like "Peeper!"

00:13:38.208 --> 00:13:40.125
We kept our end of the bargain.

00:13:40.125 --> 00:13:43.917
Just give back Professor Bitch
and it'll all be over!

00:13:45.792 --> 00:13:46.958
Wh-What the--?!

00:13:46.958 --> 00:13:49.708
The whole room... is going down?

00:13:57.542 --> 00:13:59.250
Trapping complete!

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:03.292
Doing it all at once like this
keeps the risk to a minimum.

00:14:04.375 --> 00:14:06.417
Professor Bitch!

00:14:06.417 --> 00:14:07.708
Dammit!

00:14:07.708 --> 00:14:11.542
It's all right. If he comes quietly,
no one gets killed.

00:14:11.542 --> 00:14:16.375
If we go the defiant route...
you won't get mad enough to kill?

00:14:16.375 --> 00:14:20.417
Nope. You're a little <i>too </i>scared--
even for a kid.

00:14:20.417 --> 00:14:23.250
Actually, I'm a little relieved.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.708
Here! It sounds hollow here!

00:14:25.708 --> 00:14:27.125
A shaped charge!

00:14:27.125 --> 00:14:29.208
Smoke-screen capsules!

00:14:36.417 --> 00:14:38.042
Huh!

00:14:39.958 --> 00:14:43.875
Right! Now you're talking!

00:14:43.875 --> 00:14:47.333
Now for the moment of truth.

00:14:47.333 --> 00:14:50.417
Can you hear me, E Class?

00:14:50.417 --> 00:14:54.583
The truth is, I'm very pleased you escaped.

00:14:54.583 --> 00:14:57.500
It'll be the warm-up
before the unknown big game.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.083
I expect great things from you.

00:14:59.875 --> 00:15:02.958
It's like... a game.

00:15:02.958 --> 00:15:06.958
This isn't Mr. Takaoka's simple vindictiveness.

00:15:06.958 --> 00:15:11.042
We can't see the Reaper's face.

00:15:15.792 --> 00:15:17.833
Hmm... 7 to 1.

00:15:17.833 --> 00:15:20.167
"Test Questions"
Hmm... 7 to 1.

00:15:20.167 --> 00:15:25.167
"Test Questions"
Yes, making X:Y 7 to 1 gives us a lovely math problem.

00:15:25.167 --> 00:15:26.125
"* Germany defeated Brazil 7-1"

00:15:26.125 --> 00:15:27.250
"in the 2014 FIFA World Cup semi-finals"
<i>Mineirã</i>o...

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:28.542
"in the 2014 FIFA World Cup semi-finals"
<i>Sete a un</i>...

00:15:28.542 --> 00:15:30.333
Hey, big guy!

00:15:30.333 --> 00:15:32.500
You lookin' for a fight?!

00:15:33.792 --> 00:15:36.875
I-I seem to have angered the local residents!

00:15:36.875 --> 00:15:39.125
Could there be any special circumstances?

00:15:39.125 --> 00:15:41.958
Let me just ask Maehara.
He knows a lot about soccer.

00:15:41.958 --> 00:15:45.250
The party you have dialed
is currently out of range, or--

00:15:45.375 --> 00:15:50.583
Huh? Isogai, then?
Hinata and Terasaka, too...

00:15:50.583 --> 00:15:52.042
--It's the new star we've waited for!
--I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:15:52.042 --> 00:15:53.792
--Our redeemer!
--I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:15:53.792 --> 00:15:56.958
Let's intercept him here.
No matter which way he comes from,

00:15:56.958 --> 00:15:59.167
we'll have the upper hand
if we outnumber him.

00:15:59.167 --> 00:16:01.375
Back us up, Ritsu.

00:16:01.375 --> 00:16:08.083
Don't feel like it. Not like I'm
gonna defy the Reaperman.

00:16:08.083 --> 00:16:10.542
I'd sooner turn off than do any work.

00:16:10.542 --> 00:16:13.250
She's been hacked!

00:16:17.125 --> 00:16:19.167
The Reaper...

00:16:21.542 --> 00:16:22.958
Wha--

00:16:27.708 --> 00:16:32.583
I can't make him out...
This is the skill of an assassin!

00:16:32.583 --> 00:16:35.625
--That jerk!
--He's just waltzin' right up!

00:16:38.208 --> 00:16:41.750
The first skill I honed upon
becoming an assassin

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:45.625
was head-on combat.

00:16:45.625 --> 00:16:49.917
It's 99 percent unnecessary for an assassin,

00:16:49.917 --> 00:16:53.958
but without it, the remaining
one percent of targets would get away.

00:16:53.958 --> 00:16:57.042
If you're looking to be
the world's best assassin...

00:16:57.042 --> 00:16:59.250
...it's an indispensable skill.

00:17:01.042 --> 00:17:04.417
Females are so very fragile.

00:17:04.417 --> 00:17:08.000
Can't be treating the rest of
my hostages so carelessly.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.583
Move aside, everyone.

00:17:11.917 --> 00:17:13.375
I'll take him.

00:17:13.375 --> 00:17:15.375
Nagisa...

00:17:15.375 --> 00:17:20.500
That sound was the frame of her
super P.E. clothes absorbing the impact.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:24.042
The Reaper thought it was her ribs breaking,

00:17:24.042 --> 00:17:27.417
and that that's what has me so furious.

00:17:27.417 --> 00:17:29.458
I <i>am </i>angry.

00:17:29.458 --> 00:17:34.250
My anger will quell my bloodlust
and avenge us all.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:36.625
With these two hands...

00:17:38.333 --> 00:17:39.750
Huh?

00:17:46.792 --> 00:17:50.583
Uh-oh. This won't work.

00:17:55.292 --> 00:18:00.333
The clap stunner. Yours and Lovro's
might just startle a cat.

00:18:00.333 --> 00:18:04.042
But this skill has yet another level.

00:18:04.042 --> 00:18:06.167
Human consciousness has a wavelength:

00:18:06.167 --> 00:18:10.083
the higher the peaks,
the more sensitive one is to stimulation.

00:18:10.083 --> 00:18:13.833
So when your foe's consciousness
is at its most sensitive peak,

00:18:13.833 --> 00:18:17.667
you strike with
your most powerful sound wave.

00:18:19.042 --> 00:18:23.042
That impact won't just
temporarily spook your opponent.

00:18:23.042 --> 00:18:28.042
It'll paralyze their nerves,
immobilizing them for a while.

00:18:28.042 --> 00:18:32.292
This is... top-level...

00:18:32.292 --> 00:18:35.417
So that's it, eh?

00:18:35.417 --> 00:18:36.542
Now, then... I seem to be short some people.

00:18:36.542 --> 00:18:39.542
"Second Unit: Irina Rescue Squad"
Now, then... I seem to be short some people.

00:18:42.417 --> 00:18:44.500
Professor Bitch!

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:48.208
She's breathing!

00:18:48.208 --> 00:18:49.750
Take care of Professor Bitch.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:51.958
Why do I always gotta do the dirty work?

00:18:51.958 --> 00:18:55.042
Okay, let's rendezvous
with the rest and get out of here!

00:18:55.042 --> 00:18:59.667
Got it! Gee, I'm sure glad
Professor Bitch is all right.

00:18:59.667 --> 00:19:01.083
Right?

00:19:04.833 --> 00:19:08.292
Professor... Bitch?

00:19:09.958 --> 00:19:12.958
I've been asleep for almost six months.

00:19:12.958 --> 00:19:16.250
But now I'm awake--thanks to him.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:19.083
Now to put you out of commission.

00:19:19.083 --> 00:19:20.833
Professor Bitch...

00:19:20.833 --> 00:19:22.292
Are you serious?

00:19:22.292 --> 00:19:26.375
Time for your final lesson, you brats.

00:19:28.458 --> 00:19:29.667
Ow!

00:19:29.667 --> 00:19:32.667
I stepped on a rock barefoot!

00:19:32.667 --> 00:19:34.625
Sheesh. You oka--

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:40.583
N-No fair...

00:19:40.583 --> 00:19:42.875
Acting like you were hurt...

00:19:42.875 --> 00:19:47.208
We were worried about you for... a...

00:19:47.208 --> 00:19:50.750
Such is our experience gap,
my little hatchlings.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:54.417
I've been at far more scenes of carnage.

00:19:54.417 --> 00:19:57.833
What's this? You beat them all by yourself?

00:19:57.833 --> 00:20:00.042
It's just like you said:

00:20:00.042 --> 00:20:03.458
It's worthless to throw in with these children.

00:20:03.458 --> 00:20:06.958
Exactly. They're from another world.

00:20:06.958 --> 00:20:10.250
While these children were breathing clear air,

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:13.583
we've lived our lives breathing in bloodmist.

00:20:14.625 --> 00:20:21.833
And what will <i>you </i>do?
Come quietly or fight a hopeless battle?

00:20:21.833 --> 00:20:24.833
Heh. Bring it on.

00:20:24.833 --> 00:20:28.208
Let's go, Itona.
You and me will clobber this joker!

00:20:28.208 --> 00:20:30.250
--I surrender.
--Huh?

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:32.750
He's probably on a whole other level.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:35.042
If we fight him, we'll just lose.

00:20:35.042 --> 00:20:36.583
Itona...

00:20:36.583 --> 00:20:40.625
I've learned something. We can lose today.

00:20:40.625 --> 00:20:44.375
We'll wait for our chance--until we can win.

00:20:44.375 --> 00:20:46.500
Nagisa...

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:50.708
I don't know how you're
going to try killing Koro Sensei,

00:20:50.708 --> 00:20:53.667
but will it really all go according to plan?

00:20:53.667 --> 00:20:57.625
No matter how poor my intel,
I'll still get results.

00:20:57.625 --> 00:21:00.583
That's the world's best assassin for you.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:04.542
Karasuma?

00:21:06.458 --> 00:21:08.667
How did he know?

00:21:08.667 --> 00:21:13.917
The octopus. Said if there was ever
a wall his students couldn't get over...

00:21:13.917 --> 00:21:17.625
Then it'd be his turn.

00:21:17.625 --> 00:21:19.250
This way.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:23.167
This dog disguise gives me
a natural way to track their scent!

00:21:23.167 --> 00:21:26.875
What's natural about such an overgrown mutt?

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:48.000
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:53.375
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>

00:21:53.375 --> 00:21:59.042
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:59.042 --> 00:22:04.208
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:22:04.208 --> 00:22:15.583
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:22:15.583 --> 00:22:21.167
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:22:21.167 --> 00:22:25.583
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:22:25.583 --> 00:22:32.417
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:22:32.417 --> 00:22:37.917
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:22:37.917 --> 00:22:43.417
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:43.417 --> 00:23:02.059
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>
